# B06 capture for the fade arm of the near/far body switch comparison.
# Run from the repository root with a Release build in Godot's load path:
#   BOROUGH_RENDER_PROFILE=1 godot --path src/Borough.Godot -- \
#     --ruleset rulesets/platted.toml --citizens 40000 \
#     --drive plans/evidence/far-bodies/fade/capture.drive
#
# Ticks 600-661 repeat plans/evidence/far-bodies/compare.drive so the four fixed shots and the
# 3,000-400 m approach line up with B02's grid baseline frame for frame. The camera keeps one tilt,
# heading and focus throughout.
#
# Two slow passes follow, because the chunk and the pixels change hands at different distances.
#
# Ticks 664-790, camera 900-600 m and back: the chunk residency switch. The band reaches 500 m from
# the camera to the nearest point of a 1024 m chunk, so the chunk holding the focus crosses it
# while the camera is still 700-800 m out. The pull-back repeats the steps to test the hysteresis.
#
# Ticks 900-1020, camera 560-380 m: the cross-fade itself. The dither weight is per instance and
# rises over 450-500 m from the camera to the Building, so this pass walks the ring across the
# Buildings around the focus. The draws at the end measure inside the ring against outside it.


600 ui far-windows grid
600 ui far-fade on
600 ui family-bodies on
600 roads on
600 tilt 40
600 turn right

600 focus 556 560 3000
600 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fade/3000.png
601 draw plans/evidence/far-bodies/fade/3000.tsv

602 focus 556 560 1000
602 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fade/1000.png
603 draw plans/evidence/far-bodies/fade/1000.tsv

